{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793999465,"nonce":"jMFKesI/Fts8I/4t44a34eK/C9I=","title":"Serve blinc.rs from Cloudflare instead of GitHub Pages","message":"GitHub Pages is slow to serve and its caching does not help, and the deploy step timed out in syncing_files on the first CDN-backed run (artifact 146 MiB, 1974 files). The zone is already on Cloudflare (active) and assets.blinc.rs is served from R2.\n\nPlan: Workers static assets (wrangler assets-only worker), deployed from the docs workflow.\n- Site is 1974 files, 242 MB, largest 17.7 MiB: within the 25 MiB per file and 20k file limits.\n- wrangler.jsonc with assets.directory target/site, html_handling auto-trailing-slash, not_found_handling 404-page; custom domain blinc.rs.\n- _headers: revalidate HTML, long immutable cache for hashed paths (components/releases/\u003chash\u003e/).\n- docs.yml: build uploads target/site as a normal artifact, deploy job runs wrangler deploy; needs CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN and CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID.\n- Keep the R2 externalisation of demo wasm and large assets.\n- Cutover: deploy to workers.dev and check, then swap the apex A/AAAA records for the custom domain, then disable GitHub Pages. Keep the Google verification TXT.\n- Related: 65c14ff (R2 CDN), 8276d2d (DNS to Cloudflare).","files":null}]}